Assuming he had had the opportunity to do this... what would he have done
once he reached his bag?  He would have been unable to pick up the holy
water and uncurse the stones, because he was Overloaded.

In fact, not even a wish would have saved him. ("Oops! The blessed scroll
of remove curse drops to the floor!")

Ken Arromdee has also rightly pointed out that unless the gems had been
cursed before he polymorphed them, or unless he had picked the loadstones
up, dropped them, and picked them up again, he should have been able to
simply drop the stones.

If the loadstones were, in fact, cursed, about all he'd have been able
to do is pray for a nymph to come along and steal them.

Is it just me, or does that seem unrealistic?  It seems to me that no
matter how much I'm carrying (even if I'm pinned by my backpack) I
should be able to pick up a potion long enough to #dip, no?  There's
a difference between "picking up" and "carrying"....

Interesting feature (this is in 3.1.0, don't know about later versions):
even when you're Overloaded, you can still pick up a loadstone!  (In fact
I'd hypothesize that a loadstone would be the *only* object you could
still pick up.)  Nasty.

